@meeting bridgeInvite
// The first invitation to the bridge (the user's ask, via the lead, 2026-10-17). Commander Vance at breakfast (he
// breakfasts at 06:05), the day before your first bridge hour after the first ship-wide event (Pillar 5 Step 3, seat
// C2: the bridge room is locked until you're invited; day 22 in a new game). Every reply sets flag bridge.invited, which
// the traditions engineer's bridge-hour gate reads; C2's SHIP.bridgeInvited opens the bridge doors with it. Reworded by
// head writer W2 for Step 3 (the storm behind us, the bridge itself open from now on).
title: An invitation
from: Commander Teo Vance
gist: Commander Vance: the Captain invites you to the bridge, and to bridge hour tomorrow after the day shift, on Deck 1.
== lines
vance > you: {me}. A moment. You may finish chewing.   [nod]
vance: The Captain's compliments. The storm's behind us. She has time for guests again.
vance: You're invited to the bridge. From today the doors open for you. And bridge hour, tomorrow after the day shift.
vance: Bridge hour comes once every four weeks. No regulation requires it. I approve of it anyway.
vance: Three things. Clean boots. Hands behind your back at the helm. Nothing red is to be touched.
? choice
* I'll be there.   flag:bridge.invited rel:vance+1
  vance: Good. Five minutes early is on time.
* What's up there, exactly?   flag:bridge.invited rel:vance+2
  vance: The helm, the chart table, the Captain's chair. And the best view on the ship. Don't tell Amadi I said so.
* (Say nothing)   flag:bridge.invited
  vance: I'll take that as a yes. Most people do.
vance: The Captain will say hello. She'll know your name. Don't let that unsettle you. It unsettles everyone.
vance: That's all. As you were.   [nod]
